    "description": "Previous_Status\\__c (BUILD-35) and Creation_Source_\\_c are system-maintained audit fields. No human should be able to set or change them — via record page, edit modal, inline list-view edit, quick action, import, or API-as-user. Automation must still be able to stamp them regardless of who is logged in.\n\nBuild:\n\n* Set both fields to Read Only in Field-Level Security for every non-admin profile / permission set (Rep, Ops, Manager tiers).\n\n* Set both fields to Read Only on every page layout and compact/highlights panel where they appear (layout read-only covers admins too).\n\n* Remove from any inline-editable list view column and from any screen flow input.\n\n* Verify record-triggered / autolaunched Flows and Apex still write the values: Flow and Apex run in system context and ignore FLS, so this works — but confirm with a test as a Rep user, not as admin.\n\nDesign call to confirm (recommend, don't just do):\n\n* Recommend leaving System Administrator with FLS edit but layout read-only, so bad audit data can still be corrected via API/Data Loader without a metadata deploy. Making it FLS read-only for admins too means every data fix becomes a permission change. Flag at review — Kobi's call.\n\nEffort: \\~1-2h incl. rep-user regression test.\n\nRelated: BUILD-35 (Previous Status field), BUILD-34 (Fraud Review Status record lock).\n\nSource: Kobi, 2026-08-05.",
